arguments.text:
In `middleware/body_limit.go`, `limitedReader.Read` (lines 92–99) is:

```go
func (r *limitedReader) Read(b []byte) (n int, err error) {
    n, err = r.reader.Read(b)
    r.read += int64(n)
    if r.read > r.limit {
        return n, echo.ErrStatusRequestEntityTooLarge
    }
    return
}
```

So once the cumulative count `r.read` exceeds `r.limit`, it returns the bytes read in that call (`n`, possibly > 0) together with the sentinel error `echo.ErrStatusRequestEntityTooLarge` (a `*echo.HTTPError` with Code 413, "Request Entity Too Large"). The error is returned unwrapped. The check is strictly `>`, so exactly `limit` bytes is still allowed.

